      "raw_description": "Traffic Review: Web Page Download from www.ethereal.com\n======================================================\n\nSummary\n-------\nSample capture of an ordinary web page load from a Windows XP workstation\nrunning Mozilla 1.6, recorded on 2004-05-13 at 13:17 UTC. The client\n145.254.160.237 downloads the Ethereal download page and an embedded\nGoogle advertisement. The capture contains 43 packets over 30 seconds and\nnothing malicious.\n\nPage download\n-------------\nThe client opened a TCP connection from port 3372 to www.ethereal.com\n(65.208.228.223) on port 80. The three-way handshake completed after\nabout 0.9 seconds and the client immediately sent \"GET /download.html\".\nThe Apache server answered with HTTP 200 and an 18,070-byte HTML page,\ndelivered in TCP segments of up to 1,380 bytes. The last part of the\nresponse arrived about 3.9 seconds after the request.\n\nAdvertisement\n-------------\nWhile the page was still arriving the browser looked up\npagead2.googlesyndication.com with a DNS query to the ISP resolver\n145.253.2.203. The answer pointed through two CNAME records to the\naddresses 216.239.59.104 and 216.239.59.99. The browser then opened a\nsecond TCP connection to 216.239.59.99 on port 80 and requested\n/pagead/ads with a long query string describing the ad slot. Google's\nserver replied with HTTP 200 and a 1,272-byte HTML fragment. One segment\nof that response was retransmitted and the client sent a duplicate ACK.\n\nConnection close\n----------------\nThe web server closed its connection with a FIN 13 seconds after the\npage finished loading, and the client closed its side about 12 seconds\nafter that.\n\nAssessment\n----------\nRoutine browsing. The page was served without errors and the ad request\nis expected for this site. No follow-up needed.\n"
